        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-26T23:44:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Won\u0027t there need to be a new ext4 incompat feature flag that indicates the new directory entry format is in use?",
      "revId": "4233b14c0844411511c826ca32066fc0f3c850d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6399024_9b93da16",
        "filename": "fs/ext4/super.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 3843,
      "author": {
        "id": 1045980
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-28T00:56:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no incompatibility. This used to not be allowed, so there was no directory entry format for it. New filesystems that use this will be blocked from mounting on old kernels by the previous check, and all old filesystems are automatically compatible because they cannot contain casefolded and encrypted entries. Only casefolded and encrypted entries use the extended dirents.",
      "parentUuid": "b2fa982d_afd8ad9d",
      "revId": "4233b14c0844411511c826ca32066fc0f3c850d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
